From: WPE4YDP debugging
Subject: [PATCH] WebRTC: preserve encoded key frames under appsrc backpressure

When the MediaStream playback appsrc reports enough-data, raw video frames and
encoded delta frames may be dropped. Encoded key frames must still reach the
downstream decoder; otherwise a late PLI can produce a valid IDR that is
discarded before the decoder sees it.

Also log non-OK appsrc flow returns so a stalled playback pipeline is
distinguishable from upstream packet loss.

--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerMediaStreamSource.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerMediaStreamSource.cpp
@@ -373,7 +373,11 @@ private:
 
         if (m_isVideoTrack && drop) {
             auto* caps = gst_sample_get_caps(sample.get());
-            drop = doCapsHaveType(caps, "video"_s) || GST_BUFFER_FLAG_IS_SET(buffer, GST_BUFFER_FLAG_DELTA_UNIT);
+            bool isRawVideo = doCapsHaveType(caps, "video/x-raw"_s);
+            bool isDeltaUnit = GST_BUFFER_FLAG_IS_SET(buffer, GST_BUFFER_FLAG_DELTA_UNIT);
+            drop = isRawVideo || isDeltaUnit;
+            if (!drop)
+                GST_INFO_OBJECT(m_src.get(), "Queue full; preserving encoded video key frame");
         }
 
         if (drop) {
@@ -388,7 +392,9 @@ private:
         }
 
         m_hasPushedInitialSample = true;
-        gst_app_src_push_sample(GST_APP_SRC(m_src.get()), sample.get());
+        auto flowReturn = gst_app_src_push_sample(GST_APP_SRC(m_src.get()), sample.get());
+        if (flowReturn != GST_FLOW_OK)
+            GST_WARNING_OBJECT(m_src.get(), "Failed to push sample: %s", gst_flow_get_name(flowReturn));
 
         updateStats(sample.get());
     }
